      "issue": "The claim that the blank field 'does not establish whether procedure revision or temporary instruction existed' is a limitation statement. It does not assert an event occurred (e.g., no temp instruction was issued). The evidence shows the field was blank; it does not prove absence of prior instructions because we lack records showing what, if any, revisions were pending before issue time.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record or testimony establishing whether a procedure revision or temporary instruction existed at the moment of work package issuance (source: IA-P02 point register for scope; WO-527 folder contents).",
      "question":"Does the work folder for WO-527 contain any attached temporary instructions, revised procedures, or notes indicating pending changes prior to 10:00 AM?"}
  },"decision":{
    "summary":"The board correctly identifies that directory IA-D01 and shift log IA-S01 do not establish valve states or interruption origin (supported). The claim about the blank attachment field is a limitation, not an event; it requires evidence of what instructions existed before issuance. No procedural breach can be confirmed without establishing both applicable requirements at preparation stage and action crossing them.",
    "evidenceUsed":["IA-I01","IA-S01","IA-P01","IA-P02"],
    "unknowns":[
      "Whether a temporary instruction or procedure revision existed prior to incident (node-6f3veo).",
      "Exact point of air interruption (source vs distribution vs receiving equipment)."],
    "alternatives":["The blank field reflects standard issue practice with no pending revisions; the pressure drop originated upstream and was not due to missing instruction.",
     "A temporary instruction existed but was lost or omitted from the folder cover."],
    "confidence":0.85}
}
